{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_tenancy_document", "label": "Tenancy", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One installation can serve several colleges. Each college is a tenant with its own database, reached at its own hostname."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant", "label": "Tenant", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A tenant is the outer boundary: nothing is shared across it. Each tenant has its own MariaDB database. Nothing in that database refers to another tenant."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_institution", "label": "Institution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Colleges that may see each other's rooms, people, or timetables are one tenant with several institutions. Colleges that must not see each other are separate tenants."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_database_isolation", "label": "Database boundary isolation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Isolation is the database boundary, not a tenant_id column. A tenant database never refers to another tenant."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_single_college_mode", "label": "Single college mode", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Default mode. MYSQL_DB names the database and TENANT_REGISTRY_DB is unset, so every request uses that database. Existing single-college installations change nothing. Migrations stay flask db upgrade."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant_registry", "label": "Tenant registry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TENANT_REGISTRY_DB names a database on the same server, reached with MYSQL_HOST, MYSQL_USER, and MYSQL_PASSWORD. The Host header selects the tenant. An unknown host returns 404 and a suspended tenant returns 503. flask db is not registered; upgrades are flask tenant upgrade."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenants_table", "label": "tenants table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Columns id, slug, hostname, db_name, status, created_at, updated_at. slug, hostname, and db_name are each unique. status is provisioning, active, or suspended."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_registry_schema", "label": "Tenant registry schema", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "core/tenancy/registry.py SCHEMA is the definition. The registry is not under Alembic. flask tenant init, or the first tenant create, creates the table."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant_cache", "label": "Tenant hostname cache", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hostname lookups are cached in the process for TENANT_CACHE_SECONDS, default 30, so a status change takes effect within that time on every worker."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant_cli", "label": "flask tenant commands", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Commands are init, create, list, upgrade (one slug or --all), set-status, and forget. Other commands need --tenant SLUG when a registry is configured, including seed run, admin create-superadmin, attendance, and db-adopt."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant_create", "label": "Tenant provisioning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tenant create registers the slug as provisioning, creates the database with utf8mb4_unicode_ci, runs every migration and the seeders, creates the Super Admin when admin username and email are given, then marks the tenant active. It refuses a slug, hostname, or database name already in use, and refuses a database that already exists. The default database name is college_timetable_<slug> with hyphens turned into underscores. If a step fails the tenant stays provisioning: forget the slug, drop the database by hand if it was created, and run create again."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_tenant_forget", "label": "Tenant forget", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tenant forget removes the registry row only. The app never drops a tenant database."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_request_routing", "label": "Tenant request routing", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "core/tenancy/request.py is the first before_request hook. It lower-cases the Host header, drops the port, and asks the registry. On a match it binds the tenant to g.tenant. /health and /static/ do not need a tenant."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_connection_settings", "label": "Tenant connection settings", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "models.db.connection_settings() opens the bound tenant database for rate limits, session lookup, the view, and the branding context processor. With a registry and no bound tenant it raises rather than falling back to MYSQL_DB."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_session_binding", "label": "Tenant session binding", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A signed-in session stores the slug it was opened on in session['tenant'], written by an after_request hook on the sign-in response. A cookie presented on another college's hostname is cleared before anything reads it. Set SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN only with the understanding that this binding, not the cookie scope, keeps sessions apart."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_mobile_devices", "label": "Tenant mobile devices", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Devices authenticate against mobile_devices in the tenant database they reach by hostname, so a device registered with one college cannot sync to another even with a valid signature."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_worker_loop", "label": "Per-tenant workers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The close-day worker, the export queue, the timetable queue, and the quality-model retrainer call core.tenancy.tenants_to_serve(app) and run once per active tenant inside tenant_context. A tenant that fails is logged and the others continue. A tenant added while the app is running is picked up on the next pass."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_upload_scoping", "label": "Per-tenant file paths", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uploads saved through utils/uploads.py go under static/uploads/<slug>/. The relative path stored in the database includes the slug, so existing URL building is unchanged. CSV exports go under UPLOAD_FOLDER/<slug>/reports. The learned timetable-quality model is read and written at <dir>/<slug>/<file> of QUALITY_MODEL_PATH. Static uploads stay unauthenticated; a file is reachable by someone who knows its name."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_health", "label": "Tenant health check", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With a registry, /health checks that the registry answers and that every active tenant database is at the head revision when REQUIRE_MIGRATED_DB is on. The first problem is reported as Tenant <slug>: .... A healthy response includes tenancy registry."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_unit_tests", "label": "Tenancy unit tests", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tests/unit/test_tenancy.py covers hostname parsing, validation, the lookup cache, session binding, path scoping, and the refusals. bind and create_app refuse a real database name in a testing app, and --tenant without a registry is refused."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_live_tests", "label": "Tenancy live tests", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tests/integration/test_tenancy_live.py needs --live-db. It builds college_timetable_ci_tenant_{registry,alpha,beta}_test, provisions two colleges, and checks migrations, seed rows, hostname routing, cross-host session anonymity, tenant upgrade --all, the close-day worker, unbound get_db_connection, and tenant forget keeping the database. config.testing.test_database_problem applies to the registry name and every bound db_name. All three databases are dropped at the end."}, {"id": "docs_tenancy_design_institutions", "label": "DESIGN_INSTITUTIONS.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cited for how several institutions share labs, halls, and visiting faculty inside one tenant."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_tenancy_database_isolation", "target": "docs_tenancy_tenant", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_tenancy_database_isolation", "target": "docs_tenancy_session_binding", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_tenancy_institution", "target": "docs_tenancy_tenant", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_tenancy_institution", "target": "docs_tenancy_design_institutions", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_tenancy_single_college_mode", "target": "docs_tenancy_tenant_registry", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_tenancy_single_college_mode", "target": "docs_tenancy_tenant", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/TENANCY.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "doc